<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sele (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sele is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, flowing about 64 kilometres from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-salerno">Gulf of Salerno</a>. The Greek colony of Poseidonia, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paestum">Paestum</a>, stood on the plain south of its mouth, where an important sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a>, the Heraion at Foce del Sele, was excavated in the 1930s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sele-river.jpg" alt="Sele (river)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Liberotag73 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sele_river.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
